.TH PPAK 1 "" "ppak" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ppak \- pack a directory tree into a Promptuarium container, and unpack it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ppak pack
.I DIRECTORY FILE
.br
.B ppak unpack
.I FILE DIRECTORY
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.br
.B ppak list
.I FILE
.br
.B ppak verify
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ppak
packs the contents of a directory (the files, the directories and the symbolic links, with the size and the CRC\-32
of every file, the permissions, the owners, the groups and the times) into a single Promptuarium container, signed
.BR PRMT:PPAK1\-LE ,
and unpacks it. The format is specified in PPAK_FORMAT.md (see
.BR "SEE ALSO" ).
.PP
Only the names and the contents of an archive are mandatory. An error in them (a wrong signature, an invalid or
repeated name, an entry with both a content and entries, or neither) stops
.BR ppak ,
before anything is written. Everything else is additional information: a discrepancy in it (a size or a CRC\-32 that
does not match the content, a type that contradicts it, a value that is not valid) is a warning, written to the
standard error with the path of the entry, and by default the content is used as it is.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pack \fIDIRECTORY FILE\fR
Packs the contents of the directory (not the directory itself) into the file.
.TP
.B unpack \fIFILE DIRECTORY\fR [\fB\-\-strict\fR]
Checks the whole archive, then unpacks it into the directory (created if it does not exist). With
.BR \-\-strict ,
a warning in the archive is an error, and nothing is written. Owners and groups are restored only when
.B ppak
runs as root on Linux.
.TP
.B list \fIFILE\fR
Lists the entries, like
.BR "ls \-l" .
.TP
.B verify \fIFILE\fR
Checks the archive without unpacking it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success;
.B verify
only if there is no warning.
.TP
.B 1
An error, warnings with
.BR "verify" ,
or warnings with
.BR "unpack \-\-strict" .
.TP
.B 2
Wrong usage.
.SH NOTES
Unpack into a new or empty directory: a symbolic link that is already there would be followed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppakz (1),
.BR pedit (1),
.BR file (1)
.br
https://github.com/fuszenecker/Promptuarium/blob/master/tools/PPak/PPAK_FORMAT.md
